    {
      "id": 13,
      "title": "Why there are no per-component throughput / buffer / sink panels",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 20
      },
      "targets": [

      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
        },
        "overrides": [

        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Vector's internal metrics are not available on rio.** The\n`vector-pleme-vector` self-metrics scrape target (Service\n`vector-pleme-vector` → `:9090/metrics`, Prometheus job\n`vector-pleme-vector`) is **DOWN** (`up == 0`), so **zero**\n`vector_*` series exist in VictoriaMetrics\n(`count by(__name__)({__name__=~\"vector_.+\"})` → empty).\n\nThe richer panels this dashboard would otherwise draw —\n`vector_component_received_events_total` /\n`vector_component_sent_events_total` (throughput),\n`vector_buffer_byte_size` / `vector_buffer_max_byte_size`\n(buffer fullness), `vector_component_errors_total` /\n`vector_component_discarded_events_total` (errors & drops),\n`vector_utilization` — are therefore **unobservable** until\nthat scrape is healthy.\n\n**To light them up:** ensure Vector's `internal_metrics` source\n+ a `prometheus_exporter` sink are enabled on `:9090`, and that\nthe scrape target reports `up == 1`. Until then this dashboard\ndraws the agent-liveness + cAdvisor `container_*` surface that\n*does* exist (rows below).\n"
      }
    },
